.TH expr_new 3 2026-10-23 "Graph Drawer expr man-pages 1.0.13"
.SH NAME
expr_new, expr_init, expr_free, expr_calc \- expression parser
.SH LIBRARY
Graph Drawer Expression Evaluator Library
.RI ( libexpr ,\~ \-lexpr )
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BR #include\~"expr.h"
.P
.BI "struct expr *expr_new(const char *" e ",const char *" asym ",struct expr_symset *" esp ",int " flag " ,int *" error ",char " errinfo "[EXPR_SYMLEN]);"
.BI "int expr_init(struct expr *" ep ",const char *" e ",const char *" asym ",struct expr_symset *" esp ",int " flag ");"
.BI "void expr_free(struct expr *" ep ");"
.BI "double expr_calc(const char *" e " );"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR expr_new()
function parses the expression 
.I e
and creates a
.B struct expr
object for
.BR expr_eval() .
.P
The
.BR expr_init()
function parses the expression 
.I e
and initialize an uninitialized
.B struct expr
object for
.BR expr_eval() .
.P
The
.BR expr_free()
function releases an initialized
.B struct expr
object
.IR ep .
.P
The
.BR expr_calc()
function parses the expression 
.I e
and evaluate it only once.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The
.BR expr_new()
returns the pointer to the created
.B struct expr
object. On fail, it returns
.B NULL
and sets
.I *error
and
.IR errinfo .
.P
The
.BR expr_init()
returns 0 on success. On fail, it returns -1 and sets
.I ep->error
and
.IR ep->errinfo .
.P
The
.BR expr_calc()
returns the result on success. On fail, it returns
.BR NAN .
.P
.SH NOTE
The 
.BR expr_new() , expr_init() , expr_calc()
are implemented as macros in current version. The functions actually be called are
.BR expr_new9_r() , expr_init8_r() , expr_calc5_r() .
Do not take them as function pointer.
